{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02004",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.38,
      "end_seconds": 3.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Evening. Let's get started."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 4.62,
      "end_seconds": 9.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.91,
      "end_seconds": 16.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair. How are things, what's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 18.77,
      "end_seconds": 22.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "He's been having a throbbing toothache, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.65,
      "end_seconds": 31.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.89,
      "end_seconds": 39.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.99,
      "text": "Oh, probably two days. Yeah. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.67,
      "end_seconds": 50.8,
      "duration_seconds": 10.13,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.35,
      "end_seconds": 61.07,
      "duration_seconds": 9.72,
      "text": "Hmm, it's severe, honestly. It sort of comes and goes. Hot drinks definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.51,
      "end_seconds": 65.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.81,
      "end_seconds": 70.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "It usually comes with a bad taste."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.99,
      "end_seconds": 71.95,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.73,
      "end_seconds": 79.77,
      "duration_seconds": 7.04,
      "text": "A low temperature was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.45,
      "end_seconds": 85.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Any difficulty opening the mouth, eye swelling or difficulty swallowing at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.27,
      "end_seconds": 88.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.87,
      "end_seconds": 90.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Any noisy breathing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.6,
      "end_seconds": 99.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "I haven't noticed any noisy breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.17,
      "end_seconds": 103.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.99,
      "end_seconds": 107.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Erm, no problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.86,
      "end_seconds": 114.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.13,
      "end_seconds": 118.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "No, uh, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.33,
      "end_seconds": 137.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.57,
      "end_seconds": 145.25,
      "duration_seconds": 6.68,
      "text": "Okay, uh, so it's alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 149.17,
      "end_seconds": 155.81,
      "duration_seconds": 6.64,
      "text": "Mm, that's what's prescribed, but I'm not sure he takes it every day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.69,
      "end_seconds": 166.91,
      "duration_seconds": 9.22,
      "text": "So, I'm on tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night. Paracetamol, 1 gram, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.59,
      "end_seconds": 170.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.11,
      "end_seconds": 177.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "Uh, just an operation for a hernia, last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.35,
      "end_seconds": 183.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Okay, are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.91,
      "end_seconds": 189.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Ah, no, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.35,
      "end_seconds": 202.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.55,
      "end_seconds": 209.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "My brother has epilepsy. Uh, my grandfather had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.82,
      "end_seconds": 212.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.75,
      "end_seconds": 219.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.64,
      "end_seconds": 222.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.84,
      "end_seconds": 231.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.15,
      "end_seconds": 235.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.44,
      "end_seconds": 239.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.27,
      "end_seconds": 244.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.65,
      "end_seconds": 249.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.5,
      "end_seconds": 255.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.17,
      "end_seconds": 260.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Thin bones, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.51,
      "end_seconds": 263.5,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.27,
      "end_seconds": 271.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, I've had an enlarged prostate, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.99,
      "end_seconds": 277.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "Okay, I can see thin bones in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.16,
      "end_seconds": 292.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.25,
      "end_seconds": 308.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.06,
      "end_seconds": 327.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 92, temperature is 38.7 degrees, pressure 109 over 77."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.41,
      "end_seconds": 333.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 336.66,
      "end_seconds": 337.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.23,
      "end_seconds": 342.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.09,
      "end_seconds": 359.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "The lower right molar is tender with swollen gum and the cheek is puffy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.32,
      "end_seconds": 376.18,
      "duration_seconds": 13.86,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. So where does that leave us? My working impression is a dental abscess. I'd also keep a salivary gland infection in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 377.03,
      "end_seconds": 379.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Right, is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.84,
      "end_seconds": 408.91,
      "duration_seconds": 27.07,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like a dental abscess, but I'd like to confirm. I'm going to order a dental X-ray, for dental abscess. For this, amoxicillin, 500 milligrams, three times a day, five days. You take it by mouth. It's for dental abscess. See the dentist today, rinse with warm salt water. I'm going to send a referral to the dentist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 409.44,
      "end_seconds": 421.15,
      "duration_seconds": 11.71,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. What are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 421.88,
      "end_seconds": 431.19,
      "duration_seconds": 9.31,
      "text": "So, uh, I take the amoxicillin, 500 milligrams, three times a day. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 433.03,
      "end_seconds": 438.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 440.44,
      "end_seconds": 443.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 444.72,
      "end_seconds": 446.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}